==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|been}}, {{l|en|bene}}
* {{l|en|bien}} {{qualifier|Scotland}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|been|lang=enm}}, {{term|beene|lang=enm}}, {{term|bene||gracious, generous, pleasant|lang=enm}}, of unknown origin. Perhaps from {{etyl|non}} {{term|beinn||straight, right, favourable, advantageous, convenient, friendly, fair, keen|lang=non}}, from {{proto|gem-pro|bainaz|straight|lang=en}}, from {{proto|ine-pro|bhei-|to hit, beat|lang=en}}. Cognate with {{etyl|sco|-}} {{term|bein|lang=sco}}, {{term|bien||in good condition, pleasant, well-to-do, cosy, well-stocked, pleasant, keen|lang=sco}}, {{etyl|is|-}} {{term|beinn||straight, direct, hospitable|lang=is}}, {{etyl|no|-}} {{term|bein||straight, direct, easy to deal with|lang=no}}. See also {{l|en|bain}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{context|Now|_|chiefly|dialectal}} [[wealthy|Wealthy]]; [[well-to-do]].
#: ''a '''bein''' farmer''
# {{context|Now|_|chiefly|dialectal}} Well provided; [[comfortable]]; [[cosy]].

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|beinly}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# {{context|Now|_|chiefly|dialectal}} [[comfortably|Comfortably]].

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

{{context|Scotland}}

# {{transitive}} To [[render]] or make comfortable; [[dry]].

